        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "79bae27f-a4d4-5408-a5b7-a44e7509779f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Prince of Wales Glacier, Queen Elizabeth Range, Hochstein Ridge, Kohmyr Ridge, Hamilton Glacier\n- People: Charles, Prince of Wales, Elizabeth II, Sophia of Hanover, Queen Anne\n- Organizations: New Zealand Geological Survey Antarctic Expedition\n- Topics: Antarctic place naming, British royal succession\n\nFacts:\n- Prince of Wales Glacier is a glacier in the Queen Elizabeth Range that flows generally north for about 10 nautical miles between Hochstein Ridge and Kohmyr Ridge into Hamilton Glacier.\n- The northern party of the New Zealand Geological Survey Antarctic Expedition named Prince of Wales Glacier in 1961–62 for Charles, Prince of Wales, the eldest son of Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom.\n- Sophia of Hanover, the heir presumptive to Queen Anne, died in 1714 at the age of 83.\n- Charles, Prince of Wales, is also the oldest person to be next in line to the throne since Sophia of Hanover.",
